{
    "$comment": [
        "The colour tokens: the one place a colour in the interface is written down.",
        "",
        "Read by two things that must agree. assets/theme/build-tokens.js turns it into the",
        "stylesheet (every palette x theme, plus the system-dark media query), and",
        "tests/Unit/ThemeContrastTest.php checks every text/background pair in it against",
        "WCAG AA. Neither reads the other's output, so the values shipped and the values",
        "checked cannot drift apart.",
        "",
        "A palette x theme resolves in one fixed order, later wins:",
        "  base.light -> base.dark (dark only) -> palette.light -> palette.dark (dark only)",
        "",
        "A value of the form \"@name\" is a reference to another token in the same resolved",
        "set, and is replaced by that token's literal value. It is resolved here, at build",
        "time, rather than written as var(--name): a chart reads these through",
        "getComputedStyle, which hands a canvas the var() unresolved.",
        "",
        "Hex values are the Claude Design prototype's, except where the prototype failed",
        "AA. Those keep their hue and move in lightness: Phase 18 section I lists the ones",
        "known up front; the contrast test found the rest (light --faint on surface-2, the",
        "light rails' and paper/ocean dark rails' --rail-faint, three light chart series,",
        "and midnight's and ocean-dark's accent-hover, which darkened under a dark ink).",
        "--focus-ring, --border-control and --border-field are additions the prototype did",
        "not have, as are the --avatar-N tones a member's placeholder is drawn in (see",
        "App\\Support\\AvatarTone). --border-field is the edge of a text field, select or",
        "textarea only; it is lighter by choice and not held to 3:1 (see ThemeContrastTest).",
        "--qr-plate is the field behind the two-factor QR code: white in every palette and",
        "theme and never overridden, because a camera reads dark modules on a light field and",
        "an inverted code fails on many phones. ThemeContrastTest holds it to that.",
        "",
        "Shape and type are not here. They do not vary by palette or theme and have no",
        "contrast to check, so they stay in assets/css/tokens.css."
    ],

